  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLyTYAM7dBkZR",
      "title": "feat: Add FMA for Super ZK Dispute Game",
      "author": "0xarktos",
      "number": 381,
      "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nExtends the existing ZK Dispute Game failure mode analysis to cover the `SuperZKDisputeGame`, the ZK-proof variant adapted for the interop superchain that commits to a super root over all chains rather than a single-chain output root.\r\n\r\n### Changes\r\n\r\n- **Updated existing FMs (FM1–FM9)** for the superchain context: aggregation circuit covering all chains, multi-chain monitoring surface, variable-length `extraData`, full-superchain proving costs.\r\n- **Added FM10**: Anchor State Type Mismatch on First Super Game (migration risk).\r\n- **Added FM11**: Partial Chain Monitoring Allows Fraudulent Output Root to Stand.\r\n- **Added FM12**: Shared Parameter Drift as Superchain Scales (operational counterpart to FM7, triggered by chain set evolution).\r\n- **Merged** the old FM6 (CWIA encoding mismatch) and a draft FM10 (variable extraData offset corruption) into a single FM6 covering the full encode / decode / validate chain.\r\n- **Merged** the old FM5 (Prestate Mismatch) with a draft FM13 (Chain Set or STF Change) into a single FM5 with three root-cause sub-cases.\r\n- Replaced all undefined abbreviations (`SZKDG`, `SFDG`, `SPDG`, `ASR`) with their full contract names and defined `VKey`, `STF`, `CWIA`, `TVL` on first use.\r\n- Updated audit requirements and the consolidated Action Items table.\r\n\r\nFor an easier to view diff see [here](https://www.diffchecker.com/KRt1hsip/)\r\n\r\n- TODO: Update spec references once the `SuperZKDisputeGame` spec gets merged.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/design-docs",
      "createdAt": "2026-05-19T10:26:18Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 362,
      "deletions": 270
    },
